-- Passage rg4-authors-purpose-p02
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('7afd5bf6-6d23-5e39-8857-49aa7db760e7', 'rg4-authors-purpose-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-authors-purpose'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Windy Kite Festival$q$, $q$Account 1: A Letter from Tomas Reyes to His Grandmother

Dear Abuela,

On Saturday I flew the dragon kite you helped me build at the Harbor Park Kite Festival! The wind was so strong that the string burned my hands a little. My kite climbed higher than the flag on the pole. Then a gust spun it around, and it almost crashed into a tree. I pulled hard and saved it. Everyone near me clapped. I did not win a ribbon, but I felt proud anyway. I wish you could have seen the sky. It was full of fish, birds, and boxes in every color.

Love, Tomas

Account 2: An Article on the Harbor Park Website

The tenth Harbor Park Kite Festival took place on Saturday, May 3. Strong winds from the bay made it one of the best flying days in the festival's history. About 150 kites were flown during the day. Judges gave ribbons in three groups: biggest kite, most creative kite, and highest flyer. The prize for most creative kite went to a twelve-year-old who built a kite shaped like a sea turtle. Park workers said that some kites were damaged in the strong wind. Several kites also got stuck in trees. The festival will return next spring.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
where public.passages.status = 'draft';
