-- Passage rg4-character-setting-plot-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('0a7e0671-5c28-5eff-a62e-e5299822fd73', 'rg4-character-setting-plot-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-character-setting-plot'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Anchor Leg$q$, $q$Every year at Maple Ridge Elementary, the fourth graders ran a relay race on field day. Each team had four runners. The last runner was called the anchor, and everyone wanted that spot. The anchor crossed the finish line while the whole school cheered.

Dev Kapoor was the fastest runner in Room 12, so his team picked him as the anchor. Dev grinned all week. But at practice, something kept going wrong. Lucia, the third runner, kept dropping the baton when she passed it to him. Dev started to sigh loudly every time it happened.

On Thursday, Lucia dropped it again. Her eyes filled with tears. "I'm sorry," she whispered. "You always grab it before I'm ready."

Dev opened his mouth to complain. Then he stopped. He thought about how fast he reached back for the baton. Maybe the problem was not only Lucia.

"Let's practice it slowly," he said. "I'll keep my hand still and open. You say 'Now!' when you're about to pass it."

They practiced the handoff twenty times during recess. On field day, Lucia called "Now!" and slapped the baton into Dev's open hand. He sprinted to the finish line. Room 12 came in second, but Dev hugged Lucia first.$q$, 'draft')
