insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('f11da04a-c60d-5df1-b95c-ae7c7c003d4f', 'rg4-comparing-texts-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-comparing-texts'), null,
        '3-5', $q$A Place at the Fire$q$, $q$Text 1: The Traveler in the Snow (a story from Mongolia)

Oyuna lived with her family in a round felt tent called a ger. One cold evening, a rider appeared out of the snow. His horse was tired, and his hands were red from the wind.

Oyuna's father opened the door wide. "Come in and warm yourself," he said. Oyuna's mother poured hot milk tea. Oyuna gave the traveler the best seat, close to the stove.

The traveler stayed the night. In the morning, he thanked them and rode away. Oyuna asked, "Will we ever see him again?"

"Maybe not," said her father. "But someday we may be the ones lost in the snow."

Text 2: Open Door (a poem from Ghana)

When a stranger comes walking
down our dusty red road,
my grandmother calls out,
"Come rest, set down your load!"

We bring cool water.
We share our yam and stew.
She tells me, "A guest
is a blessing for you."

The stranger walks on.
The sun sinks low.
Our bowls are empty,
but our hearts are full.$q$, 'draft')
