   $q$Each text gives a different reason for helping a stranger. Which choice matches them correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Both texts: the stranger promises to return and visit the family again.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Text 1: the stranger will pay you back. Text 2: the stranger is a relative.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Text 1: you may need help one day too. Text 2: a guest brings a blessing.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Text 1: a guest brings a blessing. Text 2: you may need help one day too.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-texts"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Text 1: you may need help one day too. Text 2: a guest brings a blessing.$q$, $q$Oyuna's father says "someday we may be the ones lost in the snow," and the grandmother in Text 2 says "A guest is a blessing for you." Swapping these reasons gets the texts backward.$q$, 'draft', 'f11da04a-c60d-5df1-b95c-ae7c7c003d4f')
