-- Passage rg4-connections-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('91254489-611c-59aa-a1f4-eed27c2f3457', 'rg4-connections-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-connections'), null,
        '3-5', $q$A Skate Park for Rivera Springs$q$, $q$For years, kids in Rivera Springs had nowhere safe to skateboard. They rode in parking lots and on sidewalks downtown. Store owners worried that someone would get hurt, so the town passed a rule against skating on Main Street.

A ten-year-old named Tomasz Kowalski thought that was unfair. He did not want to break the rule, but he did not want to stop skating either. So he wrote a letter to the town council. In it, he asked for a skate park where kids could ride safely.

The council said the town did not have enough money. Tomasz did not give up. He and his friends held a car wash and a bake sale. They made a poster that showed their dream park. More than two hundred people signed a paper saying they wanted the park too.

When the council saw how many people cared, the members changed their minds. They agreed to pay for half the park if the community raised the rest. Families, coaches and local businesses gave money over the next year.

The skate park opened last spring. It has ramps, rails and a smooth bowl. Skaters must wear helmets, and a sign lists the park rules. Since it opened, store owners say they have not seen a single skateboard on Main Street.$q$, 'draft')
