-- Passage rg4-context-clues-p06
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('cea28810-3163-5dca-88f6-ba46337ac348', 'rg4-context-clues-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-context-clues'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Last Swimmer$q$, $q$Nia stood on the starting block and stared at the water. She was the last swimmer in the relay, and her team was behind. Her stomach felt jittery, as if it were full of hopping crickets.

Before the meet, Coach Alvarez had given the team one piece of advice. "Keep a steady pace," he had said. "If you start too fast, you'll have nothing left at the end."

Nia's teammate Rosa touched the wall, and Nia dove in. She wanted to sprint as fast as she could right away. Instead, she remembered the coach's words. She kicked smoothly and kept the same speed with every stroke.

Halfway down the pool, Nia could see the swimmer in the next lane. That girl had started very fast, but now she was slowing down. She looked exhausted, and her arms moved heavily through the water.

Nia kept going. Her pace did not falter. Her kicks stayed just as strong and even as they were at the start. She passed the other swimmer and touched the wall first.

Her teammates cheered and splashed water at her. Nia was thrilled. She pulled off her goggles, laughing with joy, and climbed out to hug Rosa.$q$, 'draft')
