   $q$According to the passage, what makes a hot air balloon rise?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The burner heats the air inside the envelope.","is_correct":true},{"text":"A motor under the basket pushes it upward.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"Cool morning air fills the big cloth bag.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"The crew lifts it from the ground with a truck.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The burner heats the air inside the envelope.$q$, $q$Paragraph 2 says the burner heats the air in the envelope and "the hot air pushes the balloon up." Cool air is what makes the balloon sink, not rise.$q$, 'draft', '52e7118e-7e36-59b0-a057-593ba36dd24d')
