   $q$In paragraph 1, the author calls hummingbirds "tiny." Which word means almost the same as "tiny"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"small","is_correct":true},{"text":"quick","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"related-not-synonym"},{"text":"bright","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unrelated-word"},{"text":"giant","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"antonym-for-synonym"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$small$q$, $q$The first sentence says hummingbirds are some of the "smallest" birds, so "tiny" and "small" are synonyms. "Giant" means the opposite.$q$, 'draft', '9d1a0fbe-e6dd-5f6b-8364-48d8ae6cf6cb')
