   $q$In the last paragraph, the bowl is "hard and shiny now, not soft and floppy." Which pair of words from this sentence are antonyms?$q$, $q$[{"text":"shiny and floppy","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unrelated-pair"},{"text":"soft and floppy","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"synonyms-for-antonyms"},{"text":"hard and shiny","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"pairs-same-side"},{"text":"hard and soft","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$hard and soft$q$, $q$The sentence contrasts how the bowl is now with how the clay used to be, and "hard" is the opposite of "soft." "Soft" and "floppy" mean almost the same thing, so they are not antonyms.$q$, 'draft', 'dd336eed-36a2-5926-b347-1e1ed06c54c6')
