insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1f73fa7e-1c17-520a-bdd3-2901fea54021', 'rg4-figurative-language-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-figurative-language'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Chess Tournament$q$, $q$Diego Ramirez had practiced chess all fall. Now it was the day of the city tournament. His hands were as cold as ice, and butterflies were dancing in his stomach.

His first opponent was a quiet girl named Hana. She moved her pieces slowly and carefully. Diego moved fast. He wanted to win in a hurry. Before long, he made a careless mistake and lost his queen. Hana won the game.

Diego sat on a bench in the hallway. His coach, Ms. Okafor, sat beside him. "Haste makes waste," she said kindly. "Hana took her time, and it paid off. Before every move, look at the whole board."

In his next game, Diego slowed down. He studied the board like a detective searching for clues. He thought about what his opponent might do next. The game was long, but he won.

By the end of the day, Diego had won three games and lost one. He did not take home the big trophy. But he did earn a ribbon for fourth place.

On the bus ride home, Diego turned the ribbon over in his hands. He felt as proud as a peacock. He had learned something more valuable than a trophy. Slow and careful thinking was his new secret weapon.$q$, 'draft')
