   $q$Read the line "Clack and clatter, clack and hum." How does the beat of this line connect to what the poem is about?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Its quiet beat sounds like the conductor checking each ticket.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-meter"},{"text":"Its steady, repeating beat sounds like train wheels on the tracks.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Its loud beat sounds like the city waking up in the morning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Its slow, uneven beat sounds like a passenger falling asleep.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-meter"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Its steady, repeating beat sounds like train wheels on the tracks.$q$, $q$The line repeats a strong, even pattern of beats, the same way wheels go "clack" over and over on a track. The beat is steady, not slow and uneven, so it does not sound like someone falling asleep.$q$, 'draft', '6f32f95f-8a6f-56d9-8d01-4caba2f9dc74')
