   $q$The bridge says, "I do not talk. I do not walk." What is surprising about this line?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The bridge says it does not talk, yet it is telling the whole poem.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is the only line in the poem that does not belong to a stanza.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It proves that someone else is secretly the speaker of the poem.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-speaker-with-character"},{"text":"It shows that the bridge is sad because it is too old to move.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The bridge says it does not talk, yet it is telling the whole poem.$q$, $q$The whole poem is in the bridge's voice, so it is surprising when the speaker says "I do not talk." The poet imagines how a bridge would speak; the line does not mean someone else is the speaker.$q$, 'draft', 'b8fb8ccc-8db6-59c5-8f03-eca7da2ef40b')
