   $q$The scene ends with a stage direction instead of a spoken line. What does this ending show?$q$, $q$[{"text":"That a narrator has stepped in to explain the lesson of the play","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-prose-and-drama"},{"text":"That the show is a success, shown through action instead of words","is_correct":true},{"text":"That the actors forgot their lines before the play was over","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"That Grandma Bea is crying because she is sad about the rain","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-character"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$That the show is a success, shown through action instead of words$q$, $q$Grandma Bea "laughs so hard that she has to wipe her eyes," so her action shows the potato show worked. She wipes her eyes from laughing, not from sadness.$q$, 'draft', 'd235f142-7dc9-5d1b-ae55-c893a4387c25')
