-- Passage rg4-story-details-inference-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('72b78d15-5e99-5b38-8d18-081af480696f', 'rg4-story-details-inference-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g4-story-details-inference'), null,
        '3-5', $q$The Crab and the Pretty Shell$q$, $q$On a sandy beach lived a hermit crab named Pell. Pell carried a shell striped with pink and gold. Every crab on the beach said it was the prettiest shell they had ever seen.

But Pell had grown. The shell pinched his legs when he walked, and he could no longer pull himself all the way inside.

"There is a bigger shell by the rocks," said an old crab named Grun. "It is plain and gray, but it would fit you well."

Pell waved his claws. "Plain and gray? Nobody would look at me twice."

So Pell kept his pretty shell. Each day he walked more slowly. He could not keep up when the other crabs raced to the water to feed.

One afternoon, a big wave rolled far up the beach. The other crabs tucked inside their shells and tumbled safely across the sand. Pell's legs stuck out, and the rough sand scraped them as he rolled.

The next morning, Pell walked to the rocks. The gray shell was still there. He slipped inside, and it fit perfectly. For the first time in weeks, he raced to the water with the others.

Grun watched him go. "Plain shell, fast crab," he said.$q$, 'draft')
